NAME
     tcpdump - watch the packets

SYNOPSIS
     tcpdump [-i IFACE] [-n] [-c COUNT] [-s LEN] [-q] [-e] [-x] [-X]
             [-w FILE]

DESCRIPTION
     tcpdump prints a line per packet as it arrives or leaves. With -w it
     writes a pcap file instead, which can be read anywhere that reads
     pcap.

OPTIONS
     -i IFACE    which interface
     -n          numbers rather than names
     -c COUNT    stop after COUNT packets
     -s LEN      keep LEN bytes of each
     -q          shorter lines
     -e          print the ethernet header too
     -x, -X      hexadecimal, with text
     -w FILE     write a pcap file

SEE ALSO
     netstat(1), ip(8), ping(1)
